From: Tal Zussman <tz2294@columbia.edu>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:54:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mm: remove read_cache_page_gfp()

There are no callers left. Point the comment on shmem_read_folio_gfp()
at mapping_read_folio_gfp() instead.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20261102-page-wrappers-v1-7-e7280bdb31f6@columbia.edu
Signed-off-by: Tal Zussman <tz2294@columbia.edu>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reviewed-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>
Cc: Matthew Wilcox (Oracle) <willy@infradead.org>
Cc: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>
Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>
Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>
Cc: Vlastimil Babka <vbabka@kernel.org>
Cc: Mike Rapoport <rppt@kernel.org>
Cc: Suren Baghdasaryan <surenb@google.com>
Cc: Michal Hocko <mhocko@suse.com>
Cc: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>
Cc: Joshua Hahn <joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com>
Cc: Byungchul Park <byungchul@sk.com>
Cc: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>
Cc: Ying Huang <ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com>
Cc: Alistair Popple <apopple@nvidia.com>
Cc: Jason Gunthorpe <jgg@ziepe.ca>
Cc: John Hubbard <jhubbard@nvidia.com>
Cc: Peter Xu <peterx@redhat.com>
Cc: Hugh Dickins <hughd@google.com>
Cc: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>
---
 include/linux/pagemap.h |  2 --
 mm/filemap.c            | 23 -----------------------
 mm/shmem.c              |  4 ++--
 3 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pagemap.h b/include/linux/pagemap.h
index a92329805acd6..305c99bad689d 100644
--- a/include/linux/pagemap.h
+++ b/include/linux/pagemap.h
@@ -962,8 +962,6 @@ struct folio *mapping_read_folio_gfp(struct address_space *, pgoff_t index,
 		gfp_t flags);
 struct page *read_cache_page(struct address_space *, pgoff_t index,
 		filler_t *filler, struct file *file);
-extern struct page * read_cache_page_gfp(struct address_space *mapping,
-				pgoff_t index, gfp_t gfp_mask);
 
 static inline struct page *read_mapping_page(struct address_space *mapping,
 				pgoff_t index, struct file *file)
diff --git a/mm/filemap.c b/mm/filemap.c
index 996f51af940a6..1c5280e66fcb4 100644
--- a/mm/filemap.c
+++ b/mm/filemap.c
@@ -4260,29 +4260,6 @@ struct page *read_cache_page(struct address_space *mapping,
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(read_cache_page);
 
-/**
- * read_cache_page_gfp - read into page cache, using specified page allocation flags.
- * @mapping:	the page's address_space
- * @index:	the page index
- * @gfp:	the page allocator flags to use if allocating
- *
- * This is the same as "read_mapping_page(mapping, index, NULL)", but with
- * any new page allocations done using the specified allocation flags.
- *
- * If the page does not get brought uptodate, return -EIO.
- *
- * The function expects mapping->invalidate_lock to be already held.
- *
- * Return: up to date page on success, ERR_PTR() on failure.
- */
-struct page *read_cache_page_gfp(struct address_space *mapping,
-				pgoff_t index,
-				gfp_t gfp)
-{
-	return do_read_cache_page(mapping, index, NULL, NULL, gfp);
-}
-EXPORT_SYMBOL(read_cache_page_gfp);
-
 /*
  * Warn about a page cache invalidation failure during a direct I/O write.
  */
diff --git a/mm/shmem.c b/mm/shmem.c
index a914ff5129daf..18890224eb384 100644
--- a/mm/shmem.c
+++ b/mm/shmem.c
@@ -6200,9 +6200,9 @@ int shmem_zero_setup_desc(struct vm_area_desc *desc)
  * @index:	the folio index
  * @gfp:	the page allocator flags to use if allocating
  *
- * This behaves as a tmpfs "read_cache_page_gfp(mapping, index, gfp)",
+ * This behaves as a tmpfs "mapping_read_folio_gfp(mapping, index, gfp)",
  * with any new page allocations done using the specified allocation flags.
- * But read_cache_page_gfp() uses the ->read_folio() method: which does not
+ * But mapping_read_folio_gfp() uses the ->read_folio() method: which does not
  * suit tmpfs, since it may have pages in swapcache, and needs to find those
  * for itself; although drivers/gpu/drm i915 and ttm rely upon this support.
  *
-- 
2.47.3

